    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.jump\n\n### Description\n\nWhen mini.jump shortcuts used with `:norm` to delete a character with `x`, it only deletes the first character it found in selected text.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.7.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open a file that has more than one line, choose a character that included on those lines ('a' will be used for example).\r\n2. Select those lines with visual mode.\r\n3. Try to run `:norm fax`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSelected character should be deleted from all selected lines.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nOnly the character in the first line that includes selected character gets deleted.\r\n\r\n![output](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/30773603/193450449-32aabb60-9bbb-46d4-ac44-ba73f508f290.gif)\r\n![output2](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/30773603/193450455-cec03432-6683-421f-95be-d19ab79fbfdd.gif)\r\n",
